From f1064367a1252e19bc84808094d9958be9fa9fa2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shivam-Sharma <shivamsharmaxd43@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 13:44:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] conformance: check the exact hook argv and add 3
 MUST-rule fixtures

The handshake check only looked at --host/--adapter-protocol, so an adapter
that sent the wrong native event (or none) passed; expectedHookEvent was
never read. New fixtures cover an unknown decision, a missing
protocolVersion and a post-action deny without updatedOutput. Each was
passed by a deliberately wrong adapter before this change.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TnQvGeyaju6t8dVH4gy5it
